# Git

## Commit format

Use Conventional Commits:

```
type(optional-scope): short summary in imperative mood
```

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`

- Subject: imperative, lowercase, no period at the end.
- Keep the subject under ~72 characters.
- Body only when the why is not obvious from the subject.
- Scope should match the module or area: `exchange`, `orders`, `auth`, `shared`, `ci`.
- **Commit only when explicitly asked** by the user.
- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Made with Cursor`, or any AI attribution trailer.
- Use only the user's configured git `user.name` / `user.email`.

## Staging discipline

- Stage only files related to the task — do not `git add .` unless the user asked.
- Do not commit unrelated local changes the user was working on.
- Do not amend or force-push unless explicitly requested.
- Before committing, verify the staged diff matches the requested change.

## When not to commit

- Exploratory changes, WIP, or partial implementations.
- Format-only changes mixed into unrelated feature work without user approval.
- Failed lint/build/test state unless the user explicitly wants a WIP commit.

---

## Examples

### 1. Commit message format

```
# ❌ BAD
fixed stuff
Update exchange page
WIP: cancel modal
feat: Added cancel exchange modal.

# ✅ GOOD
fix(exchange): handle empty buyer photos on details page
feat(exchange): add cancel exchange confirmation modal
refactor(exchange): extract exchange timeline step component
chore: bump vite to 5.4.2
```

### 2. Scope matches module

```
# ❌ BAD — vague scope for a module-specific change
fix: exchange cancel bug

# ✅ GOOD
fix(exchange): prevent double submit on cancel modal
```

### 3. Committing without user request

```
# ❌ BAD — user said "implement the modal" but did not ask to commit
git add .
git commit -m "feat(exchange): add cancel modal"

# ✅ GOOD — implement, verify, report; wait for explicit commit request
Implemented cancel modal. Lint and build passed. Say if you want me to commit.
```

### 4. Staging unrelated files

```
# ❌ BAD — stages user's unrelated WIP
git add src/modules/exchange/components/cancel-exchange-modal.tsx
git add src/modules/orders/components/orders-table.tsx  # unrelated local edit

# ✅ GOOD
git add src/modules/exchange/components/exchange-details/cancel-exchange-modal.tsx
git add src/shared/i18n/locales/ru/exchange.json
git add src/shared/i18n/locales/kz/exchange.json
git add src/shared/i18n/locales/ch/exchange.json
```

### 5. AI attribution in commit message

```
# ❌ BAD
feat(exchange): add reject modal

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
feat(exchange): add reject exchange modal
```
